{"uid":"6cdb773196a52f32","name":"test_the_v019_approach_1_incident_replayed_the_task_survives","fullName":"tests.test_progress_pin_task015#test_the_v019_approach_1_incident_replayed_the_task_survives","historyId":"44d08bcfc9a9ad7ef29cf0e86ec94dca","time":{"start":1791881270399,"stop":1791881273248,"duration":2849},"description":"`docs/roadmap.md`'s own account: v0.19 approach 1 \"was failed by\n    the stagnation guard ... after three `no_verdict` iterations that\n    pushed thirteen commits toward requirement G.2's 120 s target\n    (802.89 s -> 641.66 s) without reaching it.\" Replayed here with the\n    same shape against a stub engine: three consecutive `no_verdict`\n    iterations, thirteen real commits split 5/4/4 across them (each\n    iteration's own commits are genuinely new tree content, so the\n    fingerprint really moves and the `commit` evidence is corroborated\n    every time), and the numeric target is never reached by any of the\n    three -- the detail that made the OLD engine's `taskAbsorptionStreak`\n    forced-verify (v0.19 B.2) fire on three consecutive commit-only\n    passes regardless of whether real work was happening, and an\n    unfinished forced verify count as a strike toward failing the task.\n\n    Under THIS engine (task 013's budget-exemption already landed): the\n    default budget (`estimatedIterations` absent, so `1 + 2 == 3`) exactly\n    covers the three passes (`used` reaches exactly 3, never past it), so\n    every one of them is `budget_exempt` and the forced-verify hand-off\n    never fires; the approach's own three-strike counter never advances\n    either, because a corroborated claim resets it every pass. The task\n    survives: still `in-progress` at the end, never handed to verify,\n    all thirteen commits present in the workspace's own git history.","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>docs/roadmap.md</code>'s own account: v0.19 approach 1 &quot;was failed by<br />\nthe stagnation guard ... after three <code>no_verdict</code> iterations that<br />\npushed thirteen commits toward requirement G.2's 120 s target<br />\n(802.89 s -&gt; 641.66 s) without reaching it.&quot; Replayed here with the<br />\nsame shape against a stub engine: three consecutive <code>no_verdict</code><br />\niterations, thirteen real commits split 5/4/4 across them (each<br />\niteration's own commits are genuinely new tree content, so the<br />\nfingerprint really moves and the <code>commit</code> evidence is corroborated<br />\nevery time), and the numeric target is never reached by any of the<br />\nthree -- the detail that made the OLD engine's <code>taskAbsorptionStreak</code><br />\nforced-verify (v0.19 B.2) fire on three consecutive commit-only<br />\npasses regardless of whether real work was happening, and an<br />\nunfinished forced verify count as a strike toward failing the task.</p>\n<pre><code>Under THIS engine (task 013's budget-exemption already landed): the\ndefault budget (`estimatedIterations` absent, so `1 + 2 == 3`) exactly\ncovers the three passes (`used` reaches exactly 3, never past it), so\nevery one of them is `budget_exempt` and the forced-verify hand-off\nnever fires; the approach's own three-strike counter never advances\neither, because a corroborated claim resets it every pass. The task\nsurvives: still `in-progress` at the end, never handed to verify,\nall thirteen commits present in the workspace's own git history.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791880795099,"stop":1791880795099,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791880795100,"stop":1791880795100,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters"